From: jonaslacour <jonaslacour1@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 23:48:48 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] [Metal] Infer pointer address spaces over PHI and select
 cycles

getPhysicalPointerAddressSpace resolves a generic (AS 0) pointer from the
values it is derived from: casts, GEPs, PHI incomings, select operands, and
the pointers stored into the slot a load reads. To break cycles it cached
AS 0 for the value before recursing. That placeholder was never revised:
every value that met it during the recursion, and every value whose rule
failed (a select needed both operands known), kept AS 0 for good, which the
emitter spells `device`.

The PHI webs StructurizeCFG and mem2reg leave behind are such cycles, often
seeded with undef. In BatchLAS's complex<float> potrf CTA kernel six
`invariant.gep52.sink.i.reg2mem.*` PHIs form a nested cycle whose only
concrete sources are threadgroup (AS 3) GEPs; one of them came out `device`
and the Metal compiler rejected the shader ("assigning 'threadgroup void *'
to 'device void *' changes address space of pointer").

Solve the reachable generic pointers together instead: every one starts
unknown, is re-joined over its sources whenever one changes, and is cached
only at the fixpoint. A state only moves down the lattice unknown -> one
address space -> conflicting, so each value is revisited at most twice.
Sources with no information (undef, poison, values no rule covers) do not
constrain the join, for selects as already for PHIs. A conflict still gives
AS 0, and a conflicting PHI still reports an error, now naming the PHI.

